feat(fleetbar): Nightshift dispatch surface — propose, review, settle from FleetBar

Adds a native operator surface to Fleet Control Center for the autonomous
dispatch loop (PR #143 queue + PR #163 state machine). Until now the loop
was CLI-only; this PR makes it accessible directly from the app.

What the operator sees
- Status banner: Roadmap Popper countdown, Harbormaster queue/merging,
  last completion timestamp, and 30s refresh cadence indicator.
- Propose composer: multi-line TextEditor with "What should the fleet
  build tonight?" placeholder. Disabled when empty; clear-and-submit flow.
- Queued + In Flight: dispatches in proposed / claimed / in_progress /
  produced. Each row: intent (truncated to 100 chars), state badge,
  branch, elapsed, cost, transcript summary on the right.
- Awaiting Review: the big card. Per dispatch — full intent, summary,
  Open PR, View Transcript (routes to web dashboard until native detail
  view ships), green Approve (matches primary-action style), red Reject
  that opens an inline reason TextEditor and gates submit on non-empty
  trimmed text.
- Recent (24h): collapsed-by-default. Expands to show terminal-state rows
  with intent, cost, PR link, completion timestamp.

Wiring
- DispatchStore (new): @MainActor ObservableObject. Polls
  /dispatches?state=* + /dispatches/:id/transcript-summary +
  /popper/status + /harbormaster/status every 30s. Exposes
  propose(intent:), approve(id:), reject(id:reason:).
- FleetControlRoute: adds .nightshift case with moon.stars.fill icon,
  plus an isNative: Bool discriminator.
- FleetControlCenter: splits content into native vs embedded surface
  paths. Native surfaces render SwiftUI directly; web surfaces continue
  to route through /fleet-ui/ webview.
- FleetBarApp: adds @StateObject dispatchStore.

Daemon-side dependencies
The store fetches against documented routes from PR #143 + #163. Those
daemon routes are being shipped by parallel agents. When /dispatches
returns 404 the surface degrades gracefully with a warning banner that
names the missing PRs — no silent empty state.

Quality
- All body/caption fonts >=14pt. The only <=13pt text lives on state
  badges and banner-card eyebrows, all of which are uppercase + .bold +
  kerning >=0.6 per the FleetBar eyebrow exception.
- SF Symbols only, zero emoji-as-icon.
- Dark + light #Preview blocks on the section.
- DispatchStateRawValuesMatchProtocol pins the wire-format contract so
  daemon-side renames surface as test failures, not silent dropped rows.


